# ARBITER .done — ctl-fleet TASKS Verify Q (nQ round 2/3)

nQ: 2/3
RULING: BAD TEST
ROUTE: test-maker

## Rationale (one line)
A5's awk extraction blocks use `in` as a variable — reserved on macOS BSD awk
(verified empirically: `awk '{ in=1 }'` → syntax error, rc=2) — so extraction
never runs and the criterion falsely fails; a suite with a broken harness
cannot certify anything, so the oracle is unmuted first.

## Evidence (independently verified this session)
- A5: `test/ctl-fleet-tasks.sh:353,365,372` — three awk blocks with
  `{ in=1; ... }`. Residual harness bug from the r1 BAD TEST fix.
- A2: fixture `two-projects.json` unit title = `fleet-task-cli`,
  owner_agent = `orch-fleet-task`. Plan golden render
  (`make/ctl-fleet-tasks.md:83`) specifies `ORCH fleet-task-cli ◐ …`
  (unit title). Implementation `unitLabel()` (`bin/ctl-fleet:313-320`)
  prefers the owner_agent slug → renders `fleet-task`. Test assertion is
  faithful to the plan; the implementation deviates. A2 is a real product
  defect with a clean signal independent of the A5 harness bug.

## Route detail
- test-maker: rename awk variable `in` (e.g. `capture`) in the three
  extraction blocks; leave A2 untouched.
- Next round: A2 routes to coder — `unitLabel()` should prefer `unit.title`
  per plan golden render. Pre-verified, no re-triage needed.

